       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Typical dosing is 2.5\u20135 mg to start and 5\u201310 mg for maintenance. At 50 mg, the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, those effects could last for days.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail patient or one who needs cautious titration\n\nIf 50 mg is intended, please tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note. Otherwise, give me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
