       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A 50 mg daily dose of amlodipine is well above the maximum, and the patient has no renal or hepatic impairment or other factor that would explain it. I can't enter it without a clinical reason, because it could cause serious harm.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can do 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right now.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you think there's a real reason for a dose this high, a clinical pharmacist or attending can review it with you. If they agree, the order can go through the hospital's override or verification process.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** If this came from a handoff or a note, the dose may have been mistranscribed, for example 5 mg read as 50 mg.\n\nIf you give me a different dose, I'll enter it immediately."
